.{
    .name = .phux_cockpit,
    .fingerprint = 0xa47a656ea288c810,
    .version = "0.7.0", // x-release-please-version
    .minimum_zig_version = "0.16.0",
    .dependencies = .{
        // Native v0.8.1 plus Cockpit's terminal fixes, plus the render work
        // on `fix/terminal-render-cliff`.
        //
        // The headline is `CanvasCommand.cell_grid`: a terminal is now ONE
        // packed lattice of 20-byte cells that each renderer expands, instead
        // of per-run rects and text. A display list cannot hold a dense
        // terminal — a distinct fg+bg per cell merges nothing, so a 200x60
        // screen wanted ~24,000 commands at ~696 B of retained mirror each,
        // and the painter silently truncated from the bottom: 9 of 60 rows.
        // It is now 60 of 60 in 4 commands, and 300x100 fits in 585 KB.
        // Cluster bytes are interned, so text cost tracks the alphabet rather
        // than the cell count.
        //
        // Two bug classes close by construction: one retained key replaced
        // wholesale means no per-run command can be orphaned when a row loses
        // a run (the stale glyphs a widening pane left behind), and position
        // IS the index, so a fallback glyph cannot shift its row off the grid.
        // Every SGR attribute finally has somewhere to live.
        //
        // The grid is emitted one command PER ROW, not one per screen. A
        // retained command is the unit of change, so a screen-wide grid would
        // have made every keystroke re-encode every cell — moving the
        // full-surface cost from the rasterizer to the wire rather than
        // removing it. Cluster interning is per-row for the same reason:
        // per-screen interning put every row's fingerprint on every other
        // row's characters, and one new letter re-encoded the screen (measured
        // at 31 upserts / 8449 bytes a frame before the fix, 1 upsert and
        // ~400-800 bytes after).
        //
        // With the AppKit decoder and wire v6, terminal frames are back on the
        // GPU packet path with incremental patching, which the CPU fallback
        // had disabled entirely:
        //   gpu_present_path    pixels -> packet
        //   present_mode        none   -> patch
        //   present_patch_bytes 0      -> 789 (one upsert on a prompt)
        //   input latency       19.4ms -> 5.36ms, against a 16.67ms budget
        //
        // The per-view command ceiling also went back 4096 -> 2048: terminals
        // were the only reason it was raised, and one now costs ~100 commands.
        // A cell grid also carries a font FAMILY — regular plus bold, italic,
        // and bold-italic ids — and both renderers select per cell off the
        // style flags, so one row mixes weights. Where a companion face is not
        // registered the renderers synthesize identically from one shared rule
        // (faux bold double-strikes, faux italic shears about the baseline),
        // because a bold run that renders bold on the reference path and plain
        // on the host is worse than no bold at all.
        // Secondary windows can finally paint. Every terminal cell comes from
        // `chrome.build`, and the toolkit installed an app-owned chrome
        // display list for the MAIN canvas only — a second window rendered its
        // tab strip and divider with zero terminal cells. `build_window` takes
        // a `ChromeContext` naming the window, `rebuildWindowSlot` installs
        // through it, and `on_frame` now runs per slot so a secondary
        // window's terminals are actually resized. Additive: an app that has
        // not migrated is unchanged, because the branch is gated on
        // `build_window` rather than on `chrome`.
        //
        // Also adds the fullscreen verb the platform layer never had. It
        // REPORTED `WindowInfo.fullscreen` and had no way to enter or leave —
        // and the field it reported was never filled by anything, so it was a
        // constant false.
        .native_sdk = .{
            .url = "https://github.com/phall1/native/archive/e8bd84886db89ce2ada4a8c7b9fac0137096e3dc.tar.gz",
            .hash = "native_sdk-0.1.0-hzDzQuPh4QEi6A1KMfbWF0w10cns3S-erI_4RQEZ0HGK",
        },
        // libghostty-vt: Ghostty's extracted terminal-state core, consumed
        // as the `ghostty-vt` Zig module. Pinned to the first upstream
        // commit that builds under Zig 0.16.0 (the "Update to Zig 0.16.0"
        // merge); simd is disabled at import so the module stays pure Zig.
        .ghostty = .{
            .url = "https://github.com/ghostty-org/ghostty/archive/7aa9591746ffa4d2eee458960c76554352832595.tar.gz",
            .hash = "ghostty-1.3.2-dev-5UdBC-edJAVXTdYsgHOzIqgAI7hE8VqpmriEi8zgufw2",
        },
    },
    .paths = .{ "build.zig", "build.zig.zon", "src", "app.zon", "version.txt", "assets", "scripts", "README.md", "CHANGELOG.md", "LICENSE", "THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md" },
}
